  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [rec2100-linear](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-hdr-1/#valdef-color-rec2100-linear) is an extremely useful space for canvas applications that use floating-point color values, and should be added to [`PredefinedColorSpace`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#predefinedcolorspace). It is wide gamut, can be used with HDR, and is a linear space (which is particularly useful for physically based rendering applications).\n\nIt lines up with [kCGColorSpaceExtendedLinearITUR_2020](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coregraphics/cgcolorspace/extendedlinearitur_2020?language=objc) and with [VK_COLOR_SPACE_BT2020_LINEAR_EXT](https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/latest/man/html/VkColorSpaceKHR.html).\n\nThis space (and the other [predefined spaces](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/#predefined)) all share the same white. So, in particular, `[1,1,1]` in `rec2100-linear` is to match [`white`](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-3/#html4). This is described in the [converting colors](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#color-conversion) section, but it's worth pointing out here.",
